WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.560
Three scientists won the Nobel Prize in Medicine for developing optogenetics to control neurons with light. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 205. Carl Diceroth at Stanford shared the 2026 medicine prize with Peter Hegeman and George Nagel. The work began when Hegeman and Nagel identified Channel Rodopsin, a light-sensitive protein from green algae. Diceroth introduced the protein into rat and mouse neurons and used light polices

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:35.720
to trigger nerve signals. By turning the light on or off, researchers can activate or silence

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:41.500
specific neurons with millisecond precision. The method has mapped circuits involved in thirst,

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:49.000
fear, and parental behavior. Diceroth is 54 years old, a Howard Hughes Medical Institute investigator,

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:54.700
and a Stanford University professor who often works past midnight. After the announcement,

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.280
he made school lunches for his children before continuing interviews.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.140
The Nobel Committee noted the approach opened a new field for studying brain function.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:09.560
The Optogenetics Nobel recognizes a method that lets researchers switch individual neurons on

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:15.780
or off using light. Dysaroth's team first demonstrated the approach in living rodents by expressing

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:22.100
channel rotopsin and delivering precise light pulses. Subsequent work mapped circuits for thirst,

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.980
fear and parental care. Clinicians have begun testing related gene therapy

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:32.160
approaches in the eye to restore light responses into generative disease. The

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:36.740
precision now available raises the question of how far similar control can extend

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:42.120
to other brain regions without off-target effects. Early human trials focus on

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.600
retinal cells where light delivery is straightforward. Most people assume that

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:51.340
altering brain activity requires either drugs that flood many cells at once or

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:56.500
for electrodes that stimulate broad regions. Optogenetics works differently by inserting

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:02.180
a single gene for a light-gated ion channel into chosen neurons. When blue light reaches

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:08.400
those cells, the channel opens, sodium ions flow in, and the neuron fires an action potential

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:13.380
within milliseconds. In the original rodent experiments, the method isolated circuits

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:19.680
for thirst and fear without affecting neighboring cells. One number that stands out is the sub-millisecond

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:25.280
temporal resolution achieved in living tissue. The same principle is now being explored in human

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:32.060
retinal cells to restore vision after degeneration. Researchers at Murdoch University's Bioplastics

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:38.400
Innovation Hub combine machine learning with biochemistry to scan enzyme databases. The pipeline

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.980
predicts which enzymes can break down PFAS and microplastics by comparing structures to known

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:44.700
degraders.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:52.420
PhD candidate Joseph Boktor noted that agricultural soils contain roughly 23 times more microplastics

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.020
than oceans.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:59.120
The approach avoids over-engineering enzymes and instead mines evolutionary data already

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.100
present in nature.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.860
The review appeared in nature reviews, earth, and environment.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:10.020
Boktor emphasized that pollutants such as PFAS and microplastics mimic hormones and disrupt

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:10.540
health.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:16.720
The Food and Agriculture Organization report, status of the world's soil resources 2026,

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:20.460
was led by Isaac Larson at the University of Massachusetts.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:26.680
Hundreds of experts contributed data showing erosion outpaces soil formation in many regions.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:31.960
The report draws on recent scientific literature covering soil loss across continents.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:37.840
Larson and colleagues emphasize that current rates threaten long-term agricultural productivity.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.580
The findings highlight the need for improved soil management practices worldwide.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:49.540
RIFS Researcher Your Grad Key surveyed 6,284 residents in North Rhine, Westphalia.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.900
Support for wind projects correlated with political orientation and institutional trust.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.400
The study measured acceptance under different local conditions.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.300
Results were published through the Research Institute for Sustainability.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:07.460
The data show that trusting institutions strongly influences whether communities accept

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:13.800
new turbines. Durham University Business School researchers examine how retailers allocate personalized

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:18.800
offers. Shoppers who spend without strict budgeting received more discount codes.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:24.860
The study tracked purchasing patterns and offer distribution. Findings indicate retailers target

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:30.640
higher spending segments with tailored promotions. The pattern suggests that relaxed spending behavior

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:36.660
signals higher value to marketing algorithms. A clinical trial reported restoration of hearing in

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:42.440
participants with congenital deafness. The therapy targets specific genetic mutations affecting

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:47.940
inner ear cells. Early results showed measurable improvements in auditory thresholds.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:54.240
The study marks a milestone in gene therapy for sensory disorders. Researchers continue to monitor

00:04:54.240 --> 00:05:00.080
long-term stability of the restored hearing. A new study examines whether rotating black holes

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:06.360
extract energy through the penrose process. Supermassive black holes interact with surrounding plasma

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:12.580
and magnetic fields. The mechanism could explain high-energy output observed at the Milky Way Center.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:18.920
Researchers model neutron interactions to detect signatures of the process. The work connects

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:25.540
astrophysics with potential observations of galactic cores. A summary statement in JACC journals

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:32.020
reviewed current evidence on diet and nutrition. The paper synthesizes findings across cardiovascular

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:33.560
and metabolic outcomes.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:36.020
Authors highlight consistent patterns

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.020
in long-term dietary studies.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.940
The review provides clinicians

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.560
with an updated reference on dietary patterns.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.120
Multiple cohorts contributed data

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.940
on food groups and disease risk.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.100
The New York Times published a list

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.680
of the 100 biggest open questions in science.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:54.400
One entry, ranked number 24,

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:55.900
came from Eric Topel.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.680
The collection spans physics, biology, and earth sciences.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:03.560
The feature draws on input from multiple research communities.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:07.620
Readers can access the full list through the newspapers online platform.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.440
Pure Nutrition introduced a line of supplements targeting longevity pathways.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.000
Products include Ficetin and Alpha Keto Gliterate.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:20.020
The launch expands the company's presence in the healthy aging category.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:24.280
Formulations draw on existing research into cellular senescence.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:29.100
The company physicians the supplements as part of broader healthy aging strategies.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:35.560
The INS.PRESS reviewed historical attempts to extend lifespan from brown sequards extracts

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.320
to modern epigenetic clocks.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:45.240
The piece notes that ARPA H allocated $144 million in March 2026 for aging biomarkers.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:50.900
WHO projections show the global population over 80 will triple by 2050.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:56.340
The article contrasts investment levels with the absence of approved anti-aging drugs.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:07:02.180
drugs. It also covers early gerontology work by Ilya Mechnikov on intestinal bacteria.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:08.020
The American Society for Biochemistry and Molecular Biology published interviews with laboratory

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:14.300
heads. The series describes practices that foster productive research environments. Contributors

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:20.400
discuss resource allocation and mentorship approaches. The feature appears in ASBMB today.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:25.260
laboratory leaders emphasize clear communication and equitable access to

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:31.480
equipment. Chando Group delivered 20 papers at the 2026 IFCC Congress in

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:36.740
Perth. Topics covered skin biology and formulation science. The presentations

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:41.840
reflect ongoing internal research programs. The Congress focused on cosmetic and

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:46.180
dermatological innovation. The volume of submissions highlights the company's

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:51.820
investment in dermatological research. Andrew Huberman posted that videos of readers highlighting

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:57.520
and applying protocols from his book feel more gratifying than sales rankings. The post credits

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:02.700
a New York City reader for one video. Huberman noted the book reached number one on the New

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:08.060
York Times list. The response underscores the value readers place on practical application of

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:13.060
the material. Rhonda Patrick highlighted that short bursts of intense effort can restart

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:18.520
physical activity habits. Five-minute sessions still produce meaningful physiological signals.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:24.720
The approach lowers barriers for people rebuilding exercise routines. Patrick noted that cells

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:30.740
respond to the intensity of the signal, regardless of session length. Before we go, a follow-up report

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:36.120
on soil management practices is expected from the food and agriculture organization next quarter.

